---
import Legal from "../layouts/Legal.astro";
import { app } from "../data/site";
---

<Legal
  title="Security at AgentOS"
  description="How AgentOS separates public and private data, verifies payments, and takes reports."
  path="/security"
  updated="Final professional security and legal review remains part of launch governance."
>
  <p>
    AgentOS uses authenticated workspace access, server-side provider secrets,
    private object storage, verified payment webhooks, security headers, rate
    limits and audit records around sensitive operations.
  </p>

  <h2>Public/private separation</h2>
  <p>
    Public listing and professional-profile endpoints return explicit public
    fields. Private CRM, messages, unpublished listing data and private media
    require authenticated access.
  </p>

  <h2>Payment integrity</h2>
  <p>
    Paid access is activated by verified server-side payment/subscription
    events, not by a browser success page. Duplicate payment events are designed
    to be processed idempotently.
  </p>

  <h2>Reporting a concern</h2>
  <p>
    Use <a href={app.abuse}>Report Abuse</a> for suspicious content or
    trust-and-safety concerns, or <a href="/support">Support</a> for security
    questions. Do not submit passwords, card details or API secrets.
  </p>
</Legal>
